// TEST: Generic parameter beside a float at an integer instance (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019 @ 8:16
// ERROR-CONTAINS: Int64 + Float64 is Float64
// ============================================================================
// `x + 1.0` over `x: T` is typed `T` (functions/228). At an Int64 instance the
// value is a Float64, which the Int64-typed result would truncate, so the
// call is refused at its argument -- convert it first, `addone(Float64(3))`.
function addone(x: T) = x + 1.0
let n = addone(3)
